# dxxidlee.com: project rules

## Context
Portfolio for David (Seungmin) Lee, Communication Design at Parsons (graduating May 2027), Design Intern at McCann New York.
Target roles: product designer (new grad), design engineer, interaction designer, brand/visual designer, motion designer.
Hard deadline: live on dxxidlee.com by Thursday, October 1, 2026, 2pm ET. Speed beats polish. Ship, then refine.

## Stack (do not change)
- Astro 5, static output, deployed on Vercel from GitHub. No backend, no CMS, no UI framework unless asked.
- Self-hosted fonts via @fontsource or /public/fonts. No external font or script CDNs.
- Plain CSS in src/styles/global.css (or scoped <style> in components). No Tailwind unless asked.

## Architecture (keep these invariants)
- ALL content lives in src/data/site.js and src/data/projects.js. Components never hardcode project text, years, or links.
- ONE project template: src/pages/work/[slug].astro renders every project from its data entry. Never create per-project page files.
- src/components/Media.astro handles every image and video:
  no src = labeled placeholder at the right ratio; .mp4/.webm/.mov = muted, looped, playsinline video; else = lazy image.
- Draft gating: projects with status 'draft' render only when showDrafts is true (dev, or PUBLIC_SHOW_DRAFTS=true at build time).
  Placeholders must never appear in a production build without drafts. Preserve this when refactoring.
- Block types on project pages: full, pair, embed, text. Add new types in the template and document them at the top of projects.js.

## Media conventions
- Files at public/media/<slug>/<name>.mp4|.jpg|.webp
- Ratios: 16:10 landscape (covers, most blocks), 4:5 portrait (homepage pair, Instagram reuse), 16:9 for overviews and embeds.
- Loops: H.264 MP4, 6 to 8 s, no audio, under 4 MB. Videos play only while in view (IntersectionObserver) and never autoplay under prefers-reduced-motion.
- Full-length videos use the embed block (YouTube or Vimeo), never self-hosted.

## Copy rules
- Never use em dashes in any copy, comments, or UI text. Use commas, colons, or periods.
- Never invent facts, credits, dates, clients, or metrics. Keep [bracketed placeholders] until David supplies the real value.
- Sentence case. Plain verbs. One-line captions. No filler adjectives. Project pages stay under ~250 words.
- McCann client work is NDA: only show internal tools with dummy content unless David confirms clearance.

## Quality floor
- Test at 390px and 1440px widths. Keyboard focus visible. Semantic HTML. Alt text comes from media labels.
- Keep total JS minimal; no animation libraries unless asked. Lighthouse performance 90+ on the homepage.
- Run `npm run build` and confirm zero errors before calling a task done.

## Working style
- Before large changes, state a short plan (files touched, what changes) and wait for a go.
- Prefer small, reviewable diffs. Do not rename slugs or data fields without updating every reference.
- Do not delete or rewrite content in projects.js unless explicitly asked; design changes happen in components and CSS.
